From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: bound short firmware log events

The unified firmware log minimum includes the MCU header, event prefix
and TLV header, but omits four format bytes skipped before the log data.
A truncated event can advance data past the skb and produce a negative
clamped length for the text/relay log paths.

Include the fixed format bytes in the minimum. Also check that at least
four log bytes are available before reading the binary magic, so empty or
short legacy and unified text messages do not read beyond the payload.
Keep clamping oversized advertised lengths to the actual skb data.

Fixes: 56c8b4a4b407 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: validate firmware event lengths before parsing")
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/mt7996/debugfs.c
+++ b/mt7996/debugfs.c
@@ -1143,7 +1143,7 @@
 
 bool mt7996_debugfs_rx_log(struct mt7996_dev *dev, const void *data, int len)
 {
-	if (get_unaligned_le32(data) != FW_BIN_LOG_MAGIC)
+	if (len < 4 || get_unaligned_le32(data) != FW_BIN_LOG_MAGIC)
 		return false;
 
 	if (dev->relay_fwlog)
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -830,7 +830,7 @@
 		goto out;
 	}
 
-	if (skb->len < sizeof(*rxd) + 4 + sizeof(*tlv))
+	if (skb->len < sizeof(*rxd) + 4 + sizeof(*tlv) + 4)
 		return;
 
 	tlv = (struct tlv *)((char *)&rxd[1] + 4);
